Z||000009||spike||05-05-2000||01:21 PM||||I have heard alot about putting a sub in the front compartment (where spare goes), behind the seats, passanger side footwell, middle glove compartment, and trunk. I still have never heard someone mention my setup. Hum, must be a good idea. Definitly original. With minimal seat travel loss (max 1.25 inches). These boxes will be availiable soon.<BR>A must have for the BASS HAEDS. 2 10 inchers inside the car. Did the fiero interior come in only beige and gray. Is black another color. Tks. Mike. <P>PS I need to know to match the box with the fiero interior. My box was Gray and blended perfectly with my interior.||||reg||1
Z||000010||86SE||05-05-2000||02:16 PM||||my interior is dark grey.  Your boxes fit behind the seats?||||reg||1
Z||000011||spike||05-05-2000||05:28 PM||||The box is not behind the seats. I would like to know how many people are interested in my design. Trust me you have never seen a box like mine. Custom made by me. Fits perfectly without riping the inside of the fiero apart. The box fits so tight in its place that nothing is needed to hold it in place. I wish I could post pictures but if I did that how original would my design be. I have spent alot of time building it and I would like to build about a dozen and attend a few Fiero shows. I know that they would sell like hotcakes. The cost to build my box is 75-85 cdn. I might make a 2x12 inch box as well if anyone is interested. Again with max 1.50 inches of seat travel. This would require a little more work and would cost an additional 15-20 cdn. Tks for your help. ||||reg||1
