Z||000013||Homicidal||05-06-2000||04:07 AM||||Ditto, if you are nervous about somebody stealing the idea, patent and copyright the box make and then post some pics!||||reg||1
Z||000014||mwbackus||05-06-2000||05:14 AM||||     In order to obtain patent on an invention, you have to prove that the invention is "distinguishable from the prior art" which could pose to be a problem in the case of a speaker box.  However, you can file a letter of disclosure with the USPTO for only $10, which will at least protect you from a US infringement on your "first to invent" rights.  <BR>     The cost of actually preparing and filing a United States patent application is approximately $2,000 to $4,000.  So it is doubtful that this is a course of action that an individual would consider unless the invention was to be quite profitable.<BR>A copywrite is only used for protection of documents, software, etc..<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
